WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.520
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.690
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:11.650
What do you mean?

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.660
Exactly what I said.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.160
I no longer have anything to teach you.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.040
But Mama!

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.380
This past week, I saw the fruits of your Aikatsu for myself.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:31.670
Your abilities are at a level where you can be proud to call yourself a Sakuraba.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:36.300
Then why can't I beat Yume?

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.310
The only one who can answer that question

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.730
is you yourself.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.270
Me myself...

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.070
Yes, hello?

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:52.900
It's me.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.410
Huh? Who am I speaking to?

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.160
Moroboshi.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.950
Moroboshi... ah!

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:03.040
H-Headmaster?!

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:47.850
A request?

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:52.480
I'd like to ask you to lend your support to a local event.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.730
Understood. Then I'll return to school—

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:59.240
No, the location is closer to your home.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.320
Ask for the details when you arrive.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.040
<i>I'm not sure if I can perform well feeling like this,</i>

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:14.380
<i>but if there's even the slightest chance of making a breakthrough...</i>

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:17.920
My apologies.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.340
Sorry I had to ask you to set this up.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:28.180
It is our duty to illuminate our students' paths when they find them too dark to follow.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.190
Though in the end,

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:36.230
the road they choose to travel is up to them.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.570
Right.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:40.780
<i>Going there should serve her well.</i>

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.200
<b>Resort
Okunotani</b>

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.200
<b>Resort
Okunotani</b>

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:46.830
Spa Resort Okunotani...

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.830
Does that mean we're doing a travel show or something?

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:54.080
The benefits of this hot spring are...

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.250
I apologize for the delay.

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:00.090
L-Lily-senpai!

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:03.630
Does that mean this is your event?

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:08.720
Yes. We'll be staying overnight, 
and I'll be relying on your assistance.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:12.480
Of course. Please ask me anything you need.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.230
Um, what about everyone else?

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:20.740
There are no others. You and I will be the only ones.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.370
Look, it's Lily-chan!

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.910
It's been far too long!

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:34.000
Thank you for coming!

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:38.170
Everyone, I'm pleased to see you in good health.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:42.220
My, and who is this other girl?

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.300
Is she your attendant?

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.470
Huh? No, well...

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:51.770
Miss attendant, please take good care of Lily-chan.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:55.600
We're all Lily-chan's fans!

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.610
I-I see.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.240
What a wonderful view.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:13.200
The water quality at these springs is exceptional, so it's popular among the elderly.{it appears that the shitsu of various onsen is a thing that some people care a lot about and you would be called a filthy casual if you judged onsen by their temperature}{I guess I'm a fool for not double checking}

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:17.000
I lodged here often in my younger days.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.500
That explains why everyone recognized you.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:21.750
Now then,

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.880
please change into this.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.630
Is that a yukata?

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.060
Apparently not.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.850
As thanks for looking after me back then,

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:38.310
I periodically come to hold shows and perform maintenance around the hotel.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:43.780
Ah, I'm in heaven.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:48.700
Your hands feel so nice and cool, Lily-chan. {confirmed cold hands and warm heart}

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.990
I'm pleased to hear that.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:52.660
U-Um...

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.330
Am I being too forceful?

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:59.080
Ah yes, ah'm turning eighty-nahn. {desperately looking for CCs to confirm, she's saying she's turning 89?}{sounds like it}

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.920
That's not what I'm asking...

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:05.720
Still, is this really Aikatsu?

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.840
I thought Aikatsu was supposed to be more sparkly.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.930
Oh, like you'd know anything about that.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:19.690
You're the one who ain't sparkling here.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.280
Take a look at Lily there.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:32.660
You're like our very own goddess, Lily-chan.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:34.950
Your praise is wasted on me.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.290
See?

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.460
I-I can do that too!

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.760
<i>It's my fault I don't sparkle?</i>

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.470
<i>It couldn't be.</i>

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:54.180
Aikatsu!

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:57.680
One more time.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:00.900
Aikatsu!

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:04.860
It doesn't matter how good you can shout if your cleaning ain't worth a dime!

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.150
What do you mean?!

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.030
Take a look for yourself.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.990
That's what happens when you rush and only look forward.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:21.250
It's important to slow down and look around you too.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:28.510
Excuse me, Lily-senpai.

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:30.880
What is the matter?

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:35.850
There's this old man who keeps tongue-lashing me.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:37.390
Tongue-lashing?

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:41.140
He said that I was the one who wasn't sparkling,

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.110
and that I was rushing and only looking forward.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:48.400
It is said that with age comes wisdom.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:52.780
It's important to heed the advice of your seniors.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.530
Is it really?

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:59.700
Come along. Our next job is to set the dining room.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:01.790
Please wait!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:02.790
I'm not—

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.800
And I had it all stacked nicely too... {it's metaphor}

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.850
<i>What am I supposed to do?</i>

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.810
<i>What can I do to beat Yume?</i>

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.110
Thank you for the lesson.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.490
Nijino.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:35.660
You planning to keep at it longer?

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:36.620
Yes.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.620
Even if I went back to my room, I'd just be alone.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:43.870
Losing at Fall Fest has made me more motivated than ever!

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:47.920
Well, it's not like I want to discourage you.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.170
And also,

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.590
I'm sure Rola's working hard as we speak.

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:57.760
As her rival, I want to make sure I won't lose.

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:02.140
I see. Good for you.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.980
Don't go overboard.{do they ever play basket-ball?}

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.270
I won't!

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:09.400
All right! I'll start with ten kilometers per hour.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:15.820
One, two, Aikatsu! One, two, Aikatsu!

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.910
Good, I can handle this. Speed up!

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:24.660
Aikatsu! Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.180
Ouch...

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:39.260
Yume-chan...

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.930
You want me to force Nijino to rest?

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:49.810
Yes. She has the motivation, but even if her heart can keep up, her body can't.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.740
It seems I can no longer put off telling you.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.450
Do you recognize this idol?

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:06.460
Of course.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.620
She was one of the earliest S4 members,

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:12.670
and a top idol who brought Song Class to its current level.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:16.130
People said her voice was like a fleeting shooting star. {I don't have the script I need to check this line}{その歌声は儚い流れ星といわれた these words appear in literally like 35% of all songs ever}

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:18.470
Her name was Yukino Hotaru-san, right?

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:22.760
Yes, but her true name was...

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.600
Moroboshi Hotaru.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.600
Moroboshi?!

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:33.480
She fell from the path of an idol, and she was...

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:35.320
my older sister.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.120
Are you unable to sleep?

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:52.750
Yes...

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:55.130
Um...

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.380
What is it?

00:10:56.380 --> 00:11:01.510
I'm not sure if I'm living my life correctly.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:06.020
I've done everything I could think of,

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.310
but I still can't seem to beat Yume.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:13.270
Is the purpose of your Aikatsu to defeat someone?

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:17.150
Anna-sensei asked me the same thing. {}

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:22.240
She said "You simply need to shine in a way that only you can." {}{}

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:27.370
It appears to me that you have your answer already.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.370
But I don't understand.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:34.920
I can't see the path I'm supposed to take.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:43.590
Think that you are the best when you are up on stage. {apparently an eric clapton quote, but like before, it only seems to exist in japanese and no english speaking site has ever heard of it}{gonna minorly change this}

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:48.180
When you are off the stage, 
think that you are the worst.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:52.270
Those are the words of a world-famous guitarist.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:58.400
What you lack might well be belief in yourself.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:01.070
Belief in myself?

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:05.910
That will become the light that illuminates your path.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:11.790
As a special favor, I will provide one more.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:16.960
Rock is not a genre of music.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.050
It is a way of life.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:20.800
That's from...

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:26.680
They are the words of Japan's greatest rock artist, Uchida Eikichi-san.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:29.180
I've heard that before.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:35.350
He was a legendary artist who sang about how rock was his way of life.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:40.110
But I can't claim the same for myself.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.530
Tomorrow is the show.

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:47.030
We have to set up early in the morning, so you should turn in early.

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:49.410
Okay.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:55.540
<i>Where is the path I should be taking?</i>

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:02.300
Isn't this exciting, Kame-san?

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:04.970
Lily-chan's going to sing!

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:07.760
I'm looking forward to it, Tsuru-san.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.810
Everyone, check me out!

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:15.390
I pulled my old battle uniform out from the closet for the first time in years!

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:19.690
Ah'll be turning eighty-nahn.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.940
Lovely Lily!

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.320
Everyone is smiling so much!

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:30.910
Lily-senpai, you're singing because you want to make them smile.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.700
Why do you say that?

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:33.750
Huh?

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:40.000
I wish to stand on stage in a dress made with my heart's love from the brand I created.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.130
That's all.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:47.760
To put it simply, I sing for myself.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:52.390
For yourself?

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:54.770
Is that strange?

00:13:54.770 --> 00:14:00.690
N-No, I've just never heard anyone say it so directly before.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:03.030
It should be time.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:06.070
Oh, I'll head on!

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:13.830
Visitors of Spa Resort Okunotani, thank you for your patience!

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:17.290
It's time for Shirogane Lily's concert!

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:19.710
Yes, we've been waiting!

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:21.340
Lily-chan!

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.170
Hurry, hurry!

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:28.050
I'm sure you've heard this a million times, but we ask you to please silence your cell phone—

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:33.100
Geez, you're too into this!

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.720
Have it your way!

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:39.230
Shirogane Lily-san, the stage is yours!

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:49.450
Shirogane Lily, pouring my soul into this moment!

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:56.680
Lily-chan stole this old man's heart!

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:59.390
Wasn't she wonderful, Kame-san?

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:02.390
She sure was, Tsuru-san!

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:06.520
I heard the voice of Lily-chan's heart!

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:14.530
Lily-senpai, you can't fool me, 
saying you sing just for yourself.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:16.900
Do you still not understand?

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:23.160
A song that doesn't move oneself 
will never move the hearts of others.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:27.040
That's Lily's way of life.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:31.920
Oh! May I hear your impressions of my performance?

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.340
Not too bad.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:38.800
You are as strict as ever, Eikichi-san.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:41.510
Eikichi-san...

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:42.800
It couldn't be!

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:50.400
Did I neglect to tell you? This is the ambassador of Japan's rock scene,{these are different words}

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.820
as well as a former homeroom teacher of Song Class at Four Star Academy.

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.450
He is Uchida Eikichi-san.

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:06.450
Is my old student Anna still rocking like she means it?

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.210
M-My back! My back...

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.840
A-Are you all right?

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:19.720
Then what you said yesterday...

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:22.680
Was that you giving me advice?

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:30.060
I suppose I'll hand out today's word of advice now.

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:36.730
Lily forges down her path not for anyone else, but for herself.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:42.610
That transfers directly into her way of Aikatsu.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:48.120
What you need to do is forge forward for you yourself.

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:51.370
For me myself... {this is just to bring it all back to the beginning}

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:53.130
That is...

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:56.630
Going my way!

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.340
Going my way...

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.010
Taking my own path.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:16.520
There is no correct path to be found.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:20.530
All that exists is the path you believed in.

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:24.660
Whose words are those?

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:27.450
They're mine.

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:37.420
Everyone, thank you for everything.

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:40.510
Will you really return on your own?

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:45.550
Yes! I want to get back to 
Four Star Academy as fast as I can.

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:49.560
Come back any time you want, miss attendant!

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:54.060
Wouldn't you like to see miss attendant perform next time, Kame-san? {caps?}{the initial impression does that strike so but}

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:56.690
I certainly would, Tsuru-san.

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:59.690
Don't forget, Rola.

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:03.860
This is going my way!

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:06.700
Now go out and get on it.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.200
I will!

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:11.950
See you again, then!

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:23.260
That Rola's leaving with a totally different look on her face.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:25.090
Different in what way?

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:31.850
She looks ready to rock!

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:45.240
<i>I feel like I've finally found my own path.</i>

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:56.120
<i>I used to always sing to pass auditions and beat my rival.</i>

00:21:57.120 --> 00:22:00.250
<i>Yume is my rival. That won't change.</i>

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:03.670
<i>But from now on, I won't sing just to win!{but why isn't that a good enough reason to sing}</i>

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:09.260
Going my way.

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:12.760
Yeah, that gets me going!

00:22:17.190 --> 00:22:21.560
I'll sing for myself!

00:24:10.470 --> 00:24:12.760
What's up with those scary girls?

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:14.890
Are they challenging us to a duel?!

00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:17.220
The chief of fashion is right here! {no, she's talking about herself}

00:24:18.470 --> 00:24:20.560
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:22.310
Stylish Girl Lesson. {sounds like gaaru and not gyaru}

00:24:22.310 --> 00:24:24.480
Become the first-star idol!
